# Product docs snippets

Application code in `docs/content/` must be language-selectable with
`<SdkTabs>` and `<SdkSnippet lang="python|go|java|typescript|rust">`. Preference is
sticky in the browser; default Python.

Every English page outside the Developer reference needs a matching Simplified
Chinese page under `docs/i18n/zh-Hans/docusaurus-plugin-content-docs/current/`.
The Developer reference is English only. See `.cursor/rules/docs-i18n.mdc`.

Every docs page has a Markdown twin, built by the local docs exporter. Each new
MDX component needs an export rule in that exporter. The build fails on a
component without one. Phase P1 of the docs and skills cleanup adds the
exporter; this rule applies from then on.

Required shape: one `<SdkTabs>` wrapping `<SdkSnippet>` children (Python, Go,
Java, TypeScript; add Rust when `examples/rust` has the same sample), each
containing a fenced block in that language. Copy the pattern from an existing
page such as `docs/content/concepts/step/index.mdx`.

Do not use `### Java` / `### Go` headings, stacked fenced blocks per language,
or a single-language sample when the same API exists in other SDKs.

Exempt: `bash` / `text` fences, tables of API names, and IDL excerpts.

In prose outside fenced blocks, do not use inline backticks for API names,
methods, types, or identifiers. Use **bold** instead. See
`.cursor/rules/docs-writing.mdc`.
Use the exact SDK nouns and call sites; do not invent APIs.

Application snippets must be copied from runnable files under `examples/`.
The page must link to that example. If the example has HTTP, also link the
examples playground when the sample is catalogued there. Add the example first
when the API does not exist yet. See `.cursor/rules/docs-examples.mdc`.

Whenever runnable code for a documented design pattern or product example is
added or changed, run `cd docs && npm run generate:flow-definitions`. Review and
commit the affected JSON under `docs/src/data/flow-definitions/` in the same
change, even when the MDX import is unchanged.

Draw every Flow design diagram in docs with `DocsFlowDefinitionGraph`. It
renders Flow Definition Graph 2.0 JSON the way Dex Web's Design tab does.
Generate that JSON from a runnable file under `examples/` by adding the source
to `docs/scripts/generate-flow-definitions.sh`. Do not add Step graph images or
hand-written definitions. Every Step in such a source declares one `dex:group`
and one `dex:explanation` directive.
